Z||000012||BN Boomer||06-08-2000||12:24 PM||||Just for the record, the DEH-P77DH above is not the same unit advertised for $299 in the most recent Crutchfield catalog I have. The one in the Crutchfield catalog is the DEH-P86DHR that includes both the direct-connect wiring harness as well as the steering wheel remote control and has an MSRP of $440.<P>To be honest, I'm not much of stereo guy. Does anyone else have any input as to the differences between these two units and if the one through Crutchfield is a good buy for the money. I kind of like the plan Crutchfield's has allowing you to buy equipment from them in 4 payments using a credit card. What does the Voice Command and TV tuner on the DEH-P77DH do?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||06-08-2000||01:19 PM||||It just arrived! This is one sweet CD Receiver!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually, the DEH-P77DH <B>is</B> listed for $299 on <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-sLAjhRTgFy5/ProdSearch.asp?Search=pioneer" TARGET=_blank>Crutchfield</A>, so it's $80 cheaper at Marketplace4U.<P>AFAIK, the DEH-P86DHR is an older model (according to Pioneer's website).<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 06-08-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000014||Raydar||06-08-2000||01:22 PM||||Boomer,<BR>How old is your Crutchfield catalog?<BR>I got the Summer catalog this week. Doesn't have the 86, but does have the 77.<BR>Crutchfield doesn't carry the 86 any more. Closed 'em out real cheap, too. (They might still have a few. Try giving them a call.)<BR>Based on the info I've seen, the 77 has just about everything that the 86 does, with the exception of RDS (front panel display of encoded radio station info), and spectrum analyzer (maybe?). Has a really cool built-in crossover system.<BR>The TV tuner and Voice Commander are "add-on" boxes. The 77 just functions as a controller. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||BN Boomer||06-08-2000||04:20 PM||||Forunately I included the disclaimer "in the most recent  Crutchfield catalog I have" which would be the Winter/Spring 2000 edition.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Maybe it is a little dated. I'll be on the lookout for a new one in the mail.<P>Cliff, if you don't mind, what accesories did your radio come with? That is great price, too. Congratulations!||||reg||1
Z||000016||LarryB||06-08-2000||05:06 PM||||I got one of those closeout DEH-P86's a few months ago, it's a nice unit, mounted right up without any problem in the car and looks great in the dash.  The remote control that's optional in the P77 was bundled in and I mounted it for a while but found it pretty much useless.<P>Cliff, I'm sure you're going to be very pleased once you've installed the radio  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Monkeyman||06-08-2000||06:03 PM||||Cliff--Be sure that Marketplace4U.com is an authorized dealer.  According to Crutchfield, if they aren't, the warranty will be void.  Might just be a sales tactic, but you still might want to check into it.  I only called Crutchfield to see if they would match the price and be able to ship to the Neatherlands.  Crutchfield is a good name and I haven't heard of the other.  Not only will Crutchfield <B>not</B> price match, but they can't/won't ship over there.  Oh, well.  I tried.||||reg||1
Z||000018||KnightRyder31||06-08-2000||08:09 PM||||I work for Best Buy....I can buy any cd player for half off. I live in Michigan, just in case anyone wants a hookup...but you must live in Michigan to front me the cash.||||reg||1
Z||000019||lowCG||06-08-2000||08:29 PM||||I just bought my Pioneer unit last fall,before driving to Michigan,love it,works good with the cheap Pyramid speakers that were in the car.Nice power for that size interior.<BR>Where in MI do you live?||||reg||1
Z||000020||Cliff Pennock||06-08-2000||09:19 PM||||Monkeyman, Marketplace4U doesn't ship to the Netherlands either (or at least I would think so), I'm still in Pennsylvania!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But I can really recommend MarketPlace4U. They went out of their way making sure I got the unit in time - before I leave this saturday. I had emailed them several times about lots of things and they always replayed the very same day.<P>BN Boomer, the radio came with a slim remote control, not the steering wheel mounted one. Other than that there are no accessories (if you don't count the mounting brackets and the cables). But this radio can do a lot. It has a built-in car alarm, ignition blocker, pre-amp outs, aux in, Preset/Custom EQ, etc.<P>I'm sure I'll like it although I won't be able to receive all dutch radiostation because of the frequency spacing. In the US, radio frequencies are spaced at 0.2 Khz (so 90.7, 90.9, 91.9, etc) while in the Netherlands, frequencies are spaced at 0.05 KHz (90.70, 90.75, 90.80, etc). But since I hardly ever listen to the radio anyway, I don't mind.||||reg||7
